ime when we couldn't do  this  well people like me could white  landowning men really haven't had much  trouble voting through history but the  lineups at polling stations would have  looked very different if you went back  through time before 1960 first nations  couldn't vote without giving up their  indian status before 1950 the inuit  couldn't vote asian canadians didn't get  the right to vote until 1948 and if you  went back to 1917 basically half of the  entire country women couldn't vote  so back to today  it's a right that's easy to take for  granted and a lot of us do votes are  still being counted so the final voter  turnout still isn't known but it's not  good it may be just under 60 percent  which would make it the worst voter  turnout in a federal election ever  during this election the world watched  an entire country lose the right to vote  women or men there will be no visits to  a ballot box in afghanistan for the  foreseeable future no more fingers died  to show they'd just cast a vote and had  literally put their lives on the line  showing up to do it well they wish they  had our problems done in afghanistan  elections aren't easy they're bitter and  they're not cheap at 600 million they're  really not cheap but we might want to  avoid saying they don't have any value  even one word feels like no one got what  they wanted it's kind of fun and it  feels accurate to shrug our shoulders  and say all that for this  well maybe we're pretty much the same  country we were in 2019 maybe most of us  still feel pretty much the same way and  support the same people we did then it  feels like we've got the proof  so maybe we should try not to take that  expression of the will of the people for  granted and considering the brutal year  and a half we've all just had the fact  we're not more divided  may be a good sign  mike armstrong global news montreal  and that's global national for this  tuesday i'm donna friesen thanks for  watching hope to see you here aga